From 72d40249a3becd22331347dbd52ff7be5d666d4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konstantin Novikov <novkostya@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:26:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usbip: stub_rx: zero number_of_packets of non-isochronous
 URBs

The USB/IP protocol sets number_of_packets in CMD_SUBMIT to 0xffffffff
for non-isochronous transfers (Documentation/usb/usbip_protocol.rst),
and usbip-win2, the Windows client, does so. Linux's vhci-hcd sends 0,
which is why Linux clients don't hit this. stub_recv_cmd_submit() copies
the field into the URB through usbip_pack_pdu() whatever the pipe type,
so the URB reaches the host controller driver with number_of_packets
set to -1.

Most host controller drivers ignore the field for non-isochronous URBs,
but dwc2 sizes its per-URB state by it in _dwc2_hcd_urb_enqueue():

	dwc2_urb = dwc2_hcd_urb_alloc(hsotg, urb->number_of_packets,
				      mem_flags);

struct_size() saturates, the allocation warns and fails, and every
transfer fails with -ENOMEM:

  WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 6951 at mm/page_alloc.c:5291 __alloc_frozen_pages_noprof+0x6d8/0xe78
  ...
   _dwc2_hcd_urb_enqueue+0xc8/0x620
   usb_hcd_submit_urb+0xc0/0x8f0
   usb_submit_urb+0x1bc/0x5d8
   stub_rx_loop+0x9b8/0xb90 [usbip_host]
  usbip-host 1-1.3: submit_urb error, -12

So with such clients no device can be exported from a dwc2 host, e.g.
a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W. Zero number_of_packets for non-isochronous
pipes, the value usb_alloc_urb(0, ...) left there.

Tested on a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W (dwc2, 6.18.50) exporting a DualSense
to usbip-win2 0.9.8.1: control, interrupt and isochronous transfers
work. Linux vhci-hcd clients are unaffected: they already send 0.

Fixes: 4d7b5c7f8ad4 ("Staging: USB/IP: add host driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Konstantin Novikov <novkostya@gmail.com>
---
Notes for reviewers (not part of the commit message): dwc2 could instead
ignore number_of_packets for non-isochronous pipes; fixing it where the
value comes off the wire keeps it from reaching any HCD.

 drivers/usb/usbip/stub_rx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_rx.c b/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_rx.c
index 1e9ae57..23dc08a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_rx.c
@@ -590,6 +590,14 @@ static void stub_recv_cmd_submit(struct stub_device *sdev,
 		priv->urbs[i]->pipe = pipe;
 		priv->urbs[i]->complete = stub_complete;
 
+		/*
+		 * The protocol sets number_of_packets to 0xffffffff for
+		 * non-isochronous transfers. Host controller drivers that size
+		 * their per-URB state by it (dwc2) would fail with -ENOMEM.
+		 */
+		if (!usb_pipeisoc(pipe))
+			priv->urbs[i]->number_of_packets = 0;
+
 		/*
 		 * all URBs belong to a single PDU, so a global is_tweaked flag is
 		 * enough
-- 
